>> servings: 1

Halve the @banana{1} lengthways and halve the @dates{3}.

Add the @rolled oats{0.67%cup}, water{0.67%cup}, @milk{0.67%cup}, @ginger{1%tsp} (grated, or 0.5 tsp ground), @cinnamon{0.5%tsp} and @chia seeds{1%tbsp} to a small saucepan. Simmer gently over a low-medium heat for ~{4.5%minutes} (4–5 min), stirring occasionally, until thick and creamy.

Meanwhile, melt the @butter{1%tbsp} in a frying pan over a medium heat. Add the banana halves, cut-side down, and cook for ~{3%minutes} until golden and caramelised. Carefully flip and cook the other side.

Add the dates to the pan and cook for ~{2%minutes} on each side until softened and caramelised.

Once the porridge is thick and creamy, stir through 1 tbsp of the @greek yoghurt{2%tbsp}. If using the @egg{1} (optional), add it now and stir gently until fully incorporated. Simmer for a further ~{1%minute}, stirring continuously.

Spoon the porridge into a bowl and top with the caramelised banana and dates. Finish with the remaining Greek yoghurt, a splash of milk and a drizzle of @golden syrup{} or maple syrup and olive oil, if you fancy. Sprinkle with a pinch of Maldon salt, if you so wish.
